===Etymology===
[[poly-]] + [[diabolo|(di)abolo]], from the resemblance of a diabolo in cross-section to two right isosceles triangles joined at the vertices of their right angles

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|s|polyaboloes}}
# {{context|geometry|lang=en}} A [[polyform]] made by joining [[right]] [[isosceles]] [[triangle]]s edge to edge in various [[arrangement]]s.

